## How Long Do Coffin Nails Last  and How to Make Them Last Longer

The fill window, not the breakage rate, is the real maintenance question. Most wearers ask "how long do coffin nails last before breaking" when what they actually want to know is: how often will I be back in the salon, and what can I do between visits to keep them intact?

Acrylic coffin sets need a fill every two to three weeks as the natural nail grows and a gap opens at the cuticle end. The shape itself can last six to eight weeks across multiple fills before the extension needs replacing entirely. Gel coffin sets operate on a similar schedule  two to three weeks for a fill, slightly shorter for some wearers because gel is more flexible and can shift with nail growth more visibly. Press-ons, applied well with proper adhesive, last approximately five to seven days before lifting begins at the edges.

Breakage at the corners  the most common coffin-specific complaint  has two causes: length and C-curve. If the free edge is longer than the nail's natural strength can support (particularly for natural nail coffin shapes with no extension), corners flex and snap. The fix is shortening. If the C-curve wasn't built properly into the extension, the tip sits flat against pressure rather than arching slightly to distribute it. The fix is a better application  which usually means communicating this clearly to your tech.

Between fills: apply cuticle oil daily (it keeps the nail plate and extension junction flexible, which reduces lifting), avoid using nails as tools, and wear gloves for cleaning. For a full nail care routine that covers extension maintenance in detail, <a href='https://mirelleinspo.com/topics/nail-care-guide' target='_blank' rel='noopener'>the complete nail care guide</a> is the best reference. Also worth checking is <a href='https://www.mindbodygreen.com/articles/coffin-nail-shape' target='_blank' rel='noopener'>MindBodyGreen's extension health overview</a> for broader nail health context. For fill schedules and maintenance windows from a salon perspective, <a href='https://ai.shopauranails.com/coffin-nails' target='_blank' rel='noopener'>Aura Nails</a> has practitioner-specific guidance.

