## The Shape That Rewards the Decision to Try It

Coffin nails are not for everyone  and that's exactly what makes them interesting. The shape has a point of view. It is not the safest option on the menu, and it does not try to be. But the idea that <strong>coffin nails</strong> require a particular type of hand, lifestyle, or commitment level is one of the most persistent misconceptions in nail culture. Short coffin exists. Builder gel exists. Press-ons that hold the shape properly exist. The barriers are lower than the aesthetic suggests.

The decision is simpler than most guides make it: pick a length that fits your life right now, choose a material that suits your maintenance appetite, and bring a reference photo to the salon. The shape does the rest.

